# Git Commit Rules

## Commit Message Format

Every commit message MUST be concise yet comprehensive:

```
<type>(<scope>): <subject>

[Context] What area of the app this affects
[Problem] What issue or need this addresses
[Solution] What was implemented/changed
[Location] Key files modified
[Rationale] Why this approach was chosen
[Behavior] Expected outcome after this change
```

### Type Values

- `feat`: New feature
- `fix`: Bug fix
- `perf`: Performance improvement
- `refactor`: Code restructuring (no behavior change)
- `test`: Adding/updating tests
- `docs`: Documentation only
- `chore`: Build, config, tooling

### Scope Values

- `transcription`: Whisper/model related
- `audio`: FFmpeg/audio processing
- `ui`: Components/views
- `worker`: Web Worker changes
- `perf`: Performance infrastructure
- `rules`: Cursor rules/AGENTS.md

### Example - Source Change

```
feat(transcription): Add Fast Mode preset for 35%+ speedup

[Context] Transcription performance optimization initiative
[Problem] Current 1:1 real-time factor too slow for long videos
[Solution] Created TranscriptionModeSelector with Standard/Fast toggle
           Fast Mode auto-selects distil-whisper + disables enhancements
[Location] components/TranscriptionModeSelector.tsx (NEW)
           components/states/InspectStateView.tsx (modified)
           app/page.tsx (added transcriptionMode state)
[Rationale] UI preset reuses existing infrastructure vs service duplication
[Behavior] Users can toggle Fast Mode for English-only 5-6x faster transcription
```

### Example - Test Change

```
test(transcription): Add unit tests for TranscriptionModeSelector

[Context] Fast Mode feature test coverage
[Problem] New component lacks test coverage
[Solution] Added 12 test cases covering mode switching, state propagation
[Location] __tests__/unit/TranscriptionModeSelector.test.tsx (NEW)
[Rationale] TDD discipline requires tests before merge
[Behavior] 100% coverage on mode selector, all edge cases validated
```

## Commit Timing Rules

### MUST Commit When

1. **End of each implementation phase**
   - Phase 1 complete → commit
   - Phase 2 complete → commit

2. **Changeset exceeds 10 files**
   - Use message: `wip(<scope>): <phase> progress - <brief summary>`

3. **Before switching context**
   - Moving to different feature/fix → commit current work first

## Commit Hygiene

- NEVER commit with failing tests
- NEVER commit secrets, credentials, or .env files
- ALWAYS run `pnpm test` before committing
- ALWAYS use conventional commit format
- Keep commits atomic (one logical change per commit)

## Branch Strategy

- Feature work: `feat/fast-transcription-mode`
- Bug fixes: `fix/issue-description`
- Performance: `perf/optimization-description`

## Changelog Entry Format

When releasing, update CHANGELOG.md:

```markdown
## [X.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD

### Added
- Fast Transcription Mode (Beta) - 35-50% faster for English content

### Changed
- Model selector now respects selected mode

### Performance
- Distil-Whisper model reduces inference time by 5-6x
```
